em modeler  under getting started you can find text  driven tutorials with step-by-step  instructions ranging from how to set up  the software to how to create advanced  systems of models  here you will also find documentation  for the different sub libraries  available in system habla  after exploring the documentation center  you can go ahead and close both this  window and the welcome screen you will  now explore the modeling environment of  system modeler called model center when  starting up system modeler a blank  diagram will be displayed in the middle  of the window this is the canvas on  which models will be created surrounding  the diagram different toolbars and  browsers will help you create models for  this tutorial we'll be using a  scaled-down interface in the toolbar go  to View window layout and select modeler  this will remove several toolbars we  won't be using here you can switch  between different layouts at any time  in model center you'll find the class  browser to the left here you can find  ready-made example models under the  examples tab you will also find  pre-built parts for you to use when  modeling systems visa funds in the  packages listed in the library tab  click the arrow next to package to open  it up and explore it further the  education examples and industry example  packages contain complete models from  different educational and industrial  domains  in this tutorial we'll explore a model  from the introductory example packages  click the arrow next to it and locate  the inverted pendulum model under the  system's  sub package  double-click the inverted pendulum model  to open it the model will be opened in  the diagram view of system modeler  you can see here that the diagram  consists of four different components a  controller a motor opinion and a  pendulum between the components are also  connection lines the gray in green  connection lines indicate physical  connections the shaft of the motor forms  a solid connection to the rotational  part of the pinion while the  translational part forms a solid  connection to the cart of the inverted  pendulum the blue connection lines form  directional signal connections the  direction of the signals are indicated  by the arrow at the base of the  connection  component  census of other models and they can  themselves contain components to explore  a model behind the component you can  double-click it to enter it  explore the motor component in this way  inside the motor component you'll see a  new type of connection line a light blue  indicating an electrical connection on  the far left a variable voltage source  determines the voltage over the circuit  in the main model the signal determining  the voltage was connected to controller  on the far right an electro motoric  force component converts an electrical  current into a torque when you have  finished exploring the sub model you can  exit it by clicking the up arrow icon  it is now time to simulate the inverted  pendulum model simulate the model simply  press the play button in the toolbar  this will automatically both build and  simulate your model  the model will be sent to the simulation  environment of sister Matla called  a simulation center when running a  ready-made model one or more plots will  be directly shown in the plot window  this is known as a default stored plot  and it will be displayed immediately  after the model has been simulated the  stored plots are predefined plot setups  they indicate the most important  variables to explore in a model stored  plots are listed in the stored plot menu  on the left hand side of simulation  Center build entries indicate a default  stored plot  besides the variables found in store  plots you can access all variables in  model from the plot tab the variables  are sorted under the different  components and subcomponents you can  expand a component by clicking the small  arrow next to it add a plot of the  torque produced by the motor to do 