n simulations and you can do this by  duplicating an experiment right-click  the inverted pendulum in the experiment  browser and select duplicate  you now have two copies of the inverted  pendulum experiment the second copy has  not been simulated yet  before running the experiment switch  back to the parameters view and expand  the motor component  notice that the our parameter is  displayed in bold and the return arrow  next to the input field this indicates  that the parameter has been changed with  respect to the value in the mul click  the return arrow to reset it to the  model definition now go ahead and  simulate the duplicated experiment by  pressing the play button the default  plot angle and position for the second  simulation will open up in a new tab  compare the old experiment to the new  one  switch to the parametric plot that you  created previously by selecting the  corresponding tab  in the experiment browser you will see a  list of suggested plot variables these  correspond to recently plotted variables  click the first and the second suggested  float variable in order and the  parametric plot will appear in the plot  window  in the next tutorial we'll learn how to  create a model from scratch using  drag-and-drop before we open it up to  questions  let me quickly recap what we just did we  explored some different parts of model  center and simulation center by looking  at and included example model we looked  at things such as the documentation  center how to access model diagrams and  how to explore components of a model  then we started a simulation of the  model and plotted various variables from  that simulation and also viewed an  animation of the system so with that  let's open it up to you questions so if  you have any questions so far now is the  time to ask them thank you
 

